## Frameworks & Libraries
- Frontend stack: React 18 + TypeScript with Vite 6 (`@vitejs/plugin-react-swc`). Tailwind CSS v4 powers utilities; Framer Motion (`motion/react`) and Radix UI cover interaction patterns.
- Styling helpers: `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`, `class-variance-authority`; form/state libraries include `react-hook-form`, `cmdk`, `embla-carousel-react`, and `sonner` for toasts.
- Build tooling relies on alias resolution in `vite.config.ts` and SWC for compilation; no Storybook is present, but component usage mirrors shadcn documentation.

## Asset Management
- Design exports map to `src/assets/` (PNG snapshots) and `src/imports/` (auto-generated JSX + SVG path modules). The Vite config pre-binds Figma asset URIs to local files, so JSX can reference `figma:asset/...` identifiers.
- Runtime media (upload previews, processed imagery) flows through API URLs, while local assets focus on marketing UI.
- No CDN or image optimizer is wired into the Vite build; ensure large assets are optimized before inclusion.

