import { ExternalLink, CheckCircle } from "lucide-react";
import type { Product } from "../types/product";
```

## Styling Approach
- Tailwind v4 is bundled via `@tailwindcss/postcss` with design tokens piped through the CSS variable layer; no explicit `tailwind.config.{js,ts}` is required.
- Global RTL + typography directives live inside `@layer base` within `src/styles/globals.css`; additional animation utilities are declared in both `globals.css` and `styles/animations.css`.
- Responsive behavior relies on standard Tailwind prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, etc.) which remain in the generated utility sheet (`src/index.css`)—keep Figma breakpoints aligned with Tailwind’s default screen sizes or update via CSS variables if needed.

```198:211:src/styles/globals.css
@layer base {
  * {
    @apply border-border outline-ring/50;
  }

  html {
    direction: rtl;
  }

  body {
    @apply bg-background text-foreground;
    font-family: var(--font-family-vazirmatn);
    direction: rtl;
  }
}
```

## Project Structure
- `src/components/` holds feature components: user journey screens at the root, admin views under `components/admin/`, and base UI primitives under `components/ui/`.
- `src/imports/` mirrors Figma frames for high-fidelity marketing/illustration blocks; synchronize these when design tokens shift.
- Utilities stay under `src/utils/` (API, analytics, AI helpers) while configuration sits in `src/config/`. Styles consolidate in `src/styles/` with Tailwind entrypoint `src/index.css`.
- When exporting new Figma nodes, re-run the MCP integration so generated files land alongside existing ones, then wire them into React by referencing the exported component/function names.
